<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dominican Order</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dominican friar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dominican Order is a Catholic order of friars founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-dominic">Saint Dominic</a> in the early thirteenth century, dedicated to preaching and study. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>, Dominican friars such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartolome-de-las-casas">Bartolomé de las Casas</a> criticised the abuse and enslavement of indigenous Americans, influencing debates such as the Valladolid Controversy and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-laws">New Laws of 1542</a>.</p></div>
